|-
! '''Total cost per charge'''
| style="text-align:right;" | {{Coins|{{GEP|Death rune}}+{{GEP|Chaos rune}}+{{GEP|Fire rune|5}}+10}}
|}

To charge the trident, use the runes or coins on the trident. Assuming non-stop use (one cast every 2.4 seconds, 1,500 casts per hour), the trident costs {{NoCoins|({{GEP|Death rune}}+{{GEP|Chaos rune}}+{{GEP|Fire rune|5}}+10) * 1500|c}} per hour to use.

Fully charging an uncharged staff costs {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Death rune|2500}}+{{GEP|Chaos rune|2500}}+{{GEP|Fire rune|12500}}+25000|c}} total: 2,500 death runes, 2,500 chaos runes, 12,500 fire runes, and 25,000 coins. Players can configure the charges while the weapon is in their bank by right-clicking on Configure-Charges, as long as players have the required materials.

Any remaining charges within the trident can be removed at any time using the 'uncharge' option. This will recover '''only''' the [[runes]]; any coins used to charge it will be '''permanently lost''' when the trident is uncharged.

If lost on [[death]], only the uncharged trident will appear on the floor.

Rune substitutes, such as elemental staves or the [[Fountain of Rune]] '''cannot''' be used to charge the trident. Combination runes. such as [[lava rune]]s, as well as runes stored in a rune pouch '''can''' be used. However, a trident charged with combination runes will always return fire runes when uncharged. This may lead to a potential loss of up to {{coins|{{#expr:({{GEP|Fire rune|5}} - {{GEP|Steam rune|5}})}}}} per charge, when using steam runes.

