==Upgrading==
Players with level 59 [[Crafting]] can attach a [[magic fang]] to the trident using a [[chisel]], creating a [[trident of the swamp]]. In addition to a +10 magic attack bonus and a +3 bonus to the max hit, it also gains the ability to inflict [[venom]] on a target. However, the trident of the swamp requires using 1 [[Zulrah's scales|Zulrah's scale]] (with a cost of {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Zulrah's scales}}|c}}) instead of just 10 coins for each charge.

{{Infotable Bonuses|Trident of the Seas#Charged|Trident of the Swamp#Charged|nototals=yes}}

Players can also give an uncharged trident of the seas and 10 [[kraken tentacle]]s to [[Lieve McCracken]] to create an [[Trident of the Seas (e)|enhanced trident of the seas]], which holds 20,000 charges instead of 2,500. The same can be done with an uncharged trident of the swamp, which turns it into an [[Trident of the Swamp (e)|enhanced trident of the swamp]].

==Maximum hit==
<math>\begin{align}
 \text{Max Hit} &= \lfloor \frac{\text{MagicLevel}}{3} \rfloor - 5\\
\end{align}</math>

The base [[Maximum Magic hit|maximum hit]] dealt by the trident is dependent on the player's current [[Magic]] level, starting at 20 with level 75 Magic and increasing by one every three Magic levels, up to a maximum of 36 at level 123+ (obtainable only through [[smelling salts]] in [[Tombs of Amascut]]). Both magic damage bonuses and visible stat boosts will modify the max hit of the spell; likewise, stat-reductions will lower the damage. Invisible boosts, such as from the trident's attack styles, do not affect the max hit. The trident always has a max hit of at least 1, even when reduced to 0 magic. Compared to the other two powered staves, the [[trident of the swamp]] increases the base maximum hit by 3 (max of 23 at level 75), and the [[Sanguinesti staff]] increases the base maximum hit by 4 (max of 24 at level 75).

